Usage: a2m [options]

a2m — Apple ][+ / //e Enhanced emulator with integrated debugger.

    -h, --help                        show this help message and exit
    -V, --version                     print version and exit
    -A, --audio-smoke                 emit 440 Hz tone to verify audio path
    --audio-record=<str>              record runtime mono audio to WAV
    --audio-record-start=<flt>        recording start time in seconds
    --audio-record-duration=<flt>     recording duration in seconds
    -b, --break=<str>                 install execute breakpoint at hex address
    --control-port=<int>              listen on localhost TCP for A2M/13 remote control (0=off)
    --headless                        no window; short smoke exit unless --control-port is set (long-lived)
    --history-memory=<str>            CPU flight-recorder memory budget in MiB (0 or 16..4096)
    --history-off-on-max              pause CPU history while turbo is max (default on; --no-history-off-on-max)
    --inspector                       enable Inspector recording (default off; --no-inspector)
    --inspector-memory=<str>          Inspector checkpoint-ring budget in MiB (0 or 16..4096; default 128)
    -f, --defaults                    use default settings
    -d, --disk=<str>                  Disk II mount: path or s6d0=path (repeatable; same drive appends queue)
    --hd=<str>                        SmartPort mount: path or s7d0=path (repeatable; default s7d0)
    --smart=<str>                     alias for --hd
    -i, --inifile=<str>               path to an .ini file (default a2m.ini)
    --log-level=<str>                 host log policy: all|warn|error|none (default warn)
    -n, --noini                       do not use an ini file
    -!, --nosaveini                   do not save the ini no matter what
    --sna=<str>                       load machine snapshot at startup
    -m, --model=<str>                 machine model: enh (//e Enhanced) or plus (][+)
    --mb-slot=<int>                   Mockingboard slot 1..7 (default 4; 0=disable)
    --symbols=<str>                   load simple symbol file (NAME hex per line)
    -r, --remember                    add save at quit to ini file
    -v, --saveini                     save to ini file at quit
    -t, --turbo=<str>                 turbo ladder CSV: MHz and/or max (e.g. 1,max or 1,4,8,max)
    --video-display=<str>             display decoder: colour|color|white|green|amber or colour,<mono>
    --kbdjoy=<int>                    keyboard joystick on gameport stick: 0 off, 1 or 2
    --kbdjoy-layout=<str>             keyboard joystick layout: numpad or wasd

Disk/HD: repeat -d/--disk and --hd/--smart; form s6d0=path.
  Same drive twice (e.g. -d s6d0=a.nib -d s6d0=b.nib) builds a multi-image queue.
Keyboard stick: --kbdjoy 0|1|2 and --kbdjoy-layout numpad|wasd.
Display: --video-display colour|white|green|amber or colour,<mono>.
Logging: --log-level all|warn|error|none (default warn).
INI: --noini / --saveini / --remember / --defaults.

